To design the muscle coordination retraining intervention, we sought to understand the compensatory muscle activations that are necessary to generate normal walking kinetics with minimal gastrocnemius activation (Fig. 2a). We simulated healthy walking kinetics with two different static optimization objective functions: a natural coordination objective that is a surrogate for metabolic energy34,35 (Eq. 1) and a gastrocnemius avoidance objective that additionally penalizes gastrocnemius activation21 (Eq. 2).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
