Changes in plantarflexor EMG were incorporated into the static optimization simulation by constraining the simulated gastrocnemius-to-soleus activation ratio to match the ratio measured with EMG. First, a 40 ms electromechanical delay72 was added to the medial gastrocnemius, lateral gastrocnemius, and soleus EMG linear envelopes. The simulated medial gastrocnemius-to-soleus activation ratio was constrained to match the EMG ratio within 2% (Eq. 7). A similar constraint was enforced for the lateral gastrocnemius-to-soleus activation ratio.7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
